※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4612 LANG_DEFER_NOT_A_THING_TO_DO

※ What `defer` puts off runs while the block is already being left, so a way out of
※ something cannot be put off: a `return` there would leave twice.  The same goes for
※ `break`, `continue`, a `?` that hands a failure on, another `defer`, and a `let`, whose
※ name would be gone as soon as it was made.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    defer return 1u6
    0u6
